From 4dfdb3dc29eff536c27df7cd845f0503b8de72b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kara Zajac <kara@soulstone.org>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 09:35:29 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] maki: the RTC, so maki's clock keeps time

The PL031 at 0x4006_1000 was unmapped: its count read 0, so the time maki was given stood still
(the bar's clock, TOTP codes, how long since the last backup). Its DR now counts 1/1024 s in
virtual time from reset; LR loads it, CR runs it, MR's match sets RIS. No interrupt line, so
Soc's irq_cache still only watches TICKTIMER and TIMER0, and nothing has to tick it: the count
is worked out from the virtual time when it's read.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KrrQLcb6MfwT6Kc7SresSY
---
 src/bus/devices/mod.rs |   3 +
 src/bus/devices/rtc.rs | 149 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/bus/soc.rs         |   8 +++
 3 files changed, 160 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 src/bus/devices/rtc.rs

